No—but not because the wolf is incapable of fear.

The wolf walks alert. It listens, samples the air, tracks distance, remembers territory, and knows where its pack is. Night is not an unknown void to it; night is an environment its senses are built to interpret.

The wolf’s advantage is not fearlessness. It is that fear has been integrated into orientation rather than allowed to become paralysis.

Drago’s punch: the animal that believes it has nothing to fear is not the apex predator. It is the next carcass. Courage doesn’t erase threat perception; it keeps threat perception from owning the steering wheel.